  <notepads>
    <notepad>
      <note>multi_stage_pipeline - routes fifteen business documents through five chained LLM stages: classify, rate
urgency, extract details, list actions, route.
Needs Ollama at OLLAMA_URL with MODEL_NAME pulled, and the GenAI plugins with a GENAI-EE license.
Each AI Chat: Ollama ${MODEL_NAME} at ${OLLAMA_URL}, temperature 0, numCtx 4096, timeout 120,
x${STEP_COPIES}.

1. csvi-documents: CSV file input, ../multi_stage_documents.csv: document_id, source, raw_text,
   received_date.
2. const-instructions: Add constants, stage1_instruction, stage2_instruction, stage4_instruction,
   stage5_instruction.
3. ai-classify: message raw_text, instruction stage1_instruction, result stage1_json.
4. json-classify: doc_type, classification_confidence, classification_reasoning.
5. js-stage2: doc_type default general_inquiry; stage2_message = the type, then the document.
6. ai-priority: message stage2_message, instruction stage2_instruction, result stage2_json.
7. json-priority: urgency, priority, priority_reasoning.
8. js-stage3: urgency default 5, priority default MEDIUM; stage3_instruction = the JSON shape for this
   doc_type.
9. ai-extract: message raw_text, instruction stage3_instruction, result extracted_details (kept as JSON text).
10. js-stage4: extracted_details default {}; stage4_message = type, priority, urgency, then the document.
11. ai-actions: message stage4_message, instruction stage4_instruction, result stage4_json.
12. json-actions: actions, requires_escalation.
13. js-stage5: actions default ["Review manually"], requires_escalation default "false" (text);
    stage5_message = every earlier field, then the document.
14. ai-route: message stage5_message, instruction stage5_instruction, result stage5_json.
15. json-route: primary_dept, escalate_to, cc_depts, sla_hours.
16. js-finish: primary_dept default Support, escalate_to none, cc_depts [], sla_hours 48.
17. sv-results / txt-results: every stage's decision to processed_documents.csv beside this file.
Error hops: json-classify, json-priority, json-actions and json-route each send an answer they cannot parse
to their own txt-bad-&lt;stage&gt; step: document_id, that stage's JSON, err_desc to bad_&lt;stage&gt;.csv beside
this file (0 bytes when every answer parsed).

Shipped data: 15 documents, DOC-001 to DOC-015.</note>
